  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_0459560fae0a47418494d0f673f09e0f",
      "statement": "Migrations live in supabase/migrations and are ordered lexicographically by a fixed-width zero-padded timestamp filename prefix, which the migration runner relies on by collecting .sql files and sorting their paths as strings.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://deploy/inres-cli/cmd/migrate.go#L159-L179",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:46ae5e76751324bd1a36d859be6b93db9da87286ff94c4d12fb81715cb0c6d70:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3d789a8724ef47a39a1d24731dba660e",
      "statement": "The migration sequence begins with a remote schema migration that creates the pgmq schema and installs the PGMQ extension, with all later migrations applied incrementally on top.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://supabase/migrations/20250925091841_remote_schema.sql#L45-L50",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:820deb5cbdcf73b7937378cbe8d2bd8b3ccb95addd40e6260795b1d992817956:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b838cb3f330045bd85d261691dc70203",
      "statement": "The inres CLI migrate command requires DATABASE_URL, requires SUPABASE_URL unless --direct is passed, extracts the Supabase project reference from the URL by regex, and supports overriding the migrations path or listing migrations without applying them.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://deploy/inres-cli/cmd/migrate.go#L181-L195",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cfe5d763672a0b099b8d7c343710cc85792c3de043ee079aba55deca1f32aea9:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://deploy/inres-cli/cmd/migrate.go#L20-L80",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:198b317f6c1b1dd04aeda32d48a364efb1afea26760747048114e8d4194ca487:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_41030d18cd68459c9dba879f80508a8c",
      "statement": "In Kubernetes migrations run as a Helm pre-install and pre-upgrade hook Job with hook-weight -5, so they complete before any application pod starts and before other hooks, and a failure blocks the release rather than allowing pods to start against an unmigrated schema.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://deploy/helm/inres/templates/migration-job.yaml#L1-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e38388e32dc5e6cffc4f80f3a668729bd81b1e7738bcb31d44cf6e765807d7f9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bd0b47fbd6004d079a0427dd3f06c0a0",
      "statement": "The migration Job uses restartPolicy Never with a bounded backoffLimit defaulting to 3 and deletes prior jobs before creation and after success.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://deploy/helm/inres/templates/migration-job.yaml#L8-L27",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f279b9389cb4a7d7525f8c5415e8895c8dfa0658517921f68c56db40d40f9729:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_678a20cd6add46a584887781cdc3e798",
      "statement": "A separate small binary at server/api/cmd/migrate applies one hardcoded monitors migration file rather than the migration directory, so it is not the general migration mechanism.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/cmd/migrate/main.go#L36-L55",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4c681b39bcf2e0e7392ea0e91b5fcc4597274e1aa14891c6ba50125f094f727f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d2bf879d361e46b3b2962724cafff927",
      "statement": "PGMQ queues are created declaratively inside migrations with pgmq.create, and the analytics service additionally creates its queue at startup while tolerating an error because PGMQ's create is idempotent.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/services/incident_analytics_service.go#L108-L126",
